{"name":"Bambino","hex":"#8edacc","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bambino","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A child or baby, especially a representation in art of the infant Christ wrapped in swaddling clothes. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bambino"}],"entries":[{"title":"Babe Ruth","blocks":[{"text":"George Herman \"Babe\" Ruth was an American professional baseball player whose career in Major League Baseball (MLB) spanned 22 seasons, from 1914 through 1935. Nicknamed \"the Bambino\" and \"the Sultan of Swat\", he began his MLB career as a star left-handed pitcher for the Boston Red Sox, but achieved his greatest fame as a slugging outfielder for the New York Yankees. Ruth is regarded as one of the greatest sports heroes in American culture and is considered by many to be the greatest baseball player of all time. In 1936, Ruth was elected to the Baseball Hall of Fame as one of its \"first five\" members."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Babe_Ruth2.jpg/330px-Babe_Ruth2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babe_Ruth"},{"title":"Héctor Veira","blocks":[{"text":"Héctor \"Bambino\" Veira  is a former Argentine professional footballer and former coach. Since retiring as a player he has gone on to win several major titles as a manager, including the Copa Libertadores and the Intercontinental Cup, both in 1986 with River Plate. He is also considered an idol by San Lorenzo."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Bambino_veira_banfield.jpg/330px-Bambino_veira_banfield.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/H%C3%A9ctor_Veira"},{"title":"Bambino (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Bambino\" is a song recorded by Italian-French singer Dalida that became her first major hit. It was first released on 28 October 1956 as the title song of her third EP, prior to her debut album Son nom est Dalida, where it was also included. It is a French version of the Neapolitan song \"Guaglione\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c9/Bambino_EP_by_recording_artist_Dalida.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bambino_(song)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Babe_Ruth_Birthplace.JPG/500px-Babe_Ruth_Birthplace.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Babe_Ruth_Birthplace.JPG/1280px-Babe_Ruth_Birthplace.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Babe_Ruth_Birthplace.JPG/500px-Babe_Ruth_Birthplace.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ruth's birthplace in Baltimore, Maryland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABabe_Ruth_Birthplace.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/BabeRuthSr2.jpg/500px-BabeRuthSr2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/BabeRuthSr2.jpg/1280px-BabeRuthSr2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/BabeRuthSr2.jpg/500px-BabeRuthSr2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Babe Ruth's parents, George Herman Sr. and Katherine","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABabeRuthSr2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Babe_Ruth_-_St._Mary%27s_Industrial_School.JPG/500px-Babe_Ruth_-_St._Mary%27s_Industrial_School.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_cam